I don't know about the iPhone version in particular, but the Qt
build of nethack allows you to go down stairs by double-clicking
on the stairs and open non-locked or kick locked doors by double-
clicking on them.  I can easily imagine a touch-screen interface
like the one on the iPhone doing similar things.  The Qt build
*also* allows you to use the standard keys, of course, if you
know what they are, and I assume the iPhone has a way to
specify down, if you can just find out what that way is, but my
point is it's possible that a user of a non-traditional interface
might have a way to go down stairs without knowing how to
input the down direction.

The solution, of course, is to find the UI documentation for
the iPhone version of nethack (assuming said documentation
exists).


